    - build a 3x4 grid; partition all 12 cells into 3-5 polyomino pieces (4-connected) using 3 distinct non-zero colors; each color gets 1-2 pieces; ensure the partition is valid (all pieces connected, full coverage)
    - verify the solver's backtracking search finds a unique-first-hit tiling (run solver as oracle)
    - for each polyomino piece, optionally apply a random rotation/reflection
    - create a 10 x randint(10,13) grid of background 0
    - scatter the (possibly reoriented) fragments onto the grid with min L1 gap >= 2 between any pair, all cells at least 1 row/col from border
